'''<span lang="pt" dir="ltr">Lontrell</span> Denell Williams Jr.''' (born November 8, 1999), known by his stage name '''Pooh Shiesty''', is an American rapper.<ref>{{cite web|last=Jefferson|first=Devon|date=January 27, 2021|title=Who Is Pooh Shiesty? 'Black In Blood' Rapper Has The Likes Of Gucci Mane, Lil Durk, Charlamagne Tha God Hype|url=https://hiphopdx.com/news/id.60258/title.who-is-pooh-shiesty-black-in-blood-rapper-has-the-likes-of-gucci-mane-lil-durk-charlamagne-tha-god-hype|website=HotNewHipHop|access-date=February 5, 2021}}</ref> His stage name was given to him by his late brother, who adapted his childhood nickname "Mr. Pooh" with the [[African American Vernacular English|vernacular]] slang term "[[wikt:shiesty|shiesty]]", which he felt was referential of his lifestyle.<ref>{{Citation|title=Pooh Shiesty's ABCs| date=June 22, 2021 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=79rSnkxlTw8|language=en|access-date=June 22, 2021}}</ref><ref>{{Citation|title=Pooh Shiesty Tells UPROXX When He Knew "Back In Blood" Was A Hit {{!}} How I Blew Up| date=May 18, 2021 |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1aOGiE7sgDE|language=en|access-date=June 22, 2021}}</ref>

In 2020, he signed with fellow Southern rapper [[Gucci Mane]]'s [[1017 Records]], an imprint of [[Atlantic Records]], for a reported US$10 million.<ref name="XXL-Success2">{{cite web|date=December 2, 2020|title=The Break Presents: Pooh Shiesty – XXL|url=https://www.xxlmag.com/pooh-shiesty-interview-the-break/|access-date=December 2, 2020|work=[[XXL (magazine)|XXL]]}}</ref> His 2020 single, "[[Back in Blood (song)|Back in Blood]]" (featuring [[Lil Durk]]), peaked at number 13 on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]].<ref>{{cite web|last=Findlay|first=Mitch|date=November 6, 2020|title=Lil Durk Joins Pooh Shiesty on "Back in Blood"|url=https://www.hotnewhiphop.com/304185-lil-durk-joins-pooh-shiesty-on-back-in-blood-new-song|work=HotNewHipHop|access-date=November 6, 2020}}</ref> That same year, he guest appeared on the remix of [[SpotemGottem]]'s singles "[[Beat Box (SpotemGottem song)|Beat Box]]", which peaked at number 12 on the Hot 100 and remains his joint-highest entry on the chart.

His debut mixtape, ''[[Shiesty Season]]'' (2021), peaked at number three on the [[Billboard 200|''Billboard'' 200]]. He was then sentenced to five years in prison on [[firearms]] [[criminal conspiracy|conspiracy]] charges in June 2021, but was released early in late 2025. His 2025 comeback single, "[[FDO (song)|FDO]]", peaked at number 12 on the Hot 100 and became his other highest-charting song as a lead artist, tying "Beat Box 2". Following an April 2026 break-in at label boss Gucci Mane's residence, Shiesty was arrested and charged with federal conspiracy to commit kidnapping and robbery.<ref name="arr" /><ref>{{Cite web |last=Coleman II |first=C. Vernon |date=2026-08-05 |title=Pooh Shiesty Announces All Eyes on Shiest Album, Drops New Song 'Last Man Breathin' |url=https://www.xxlmag.com/pooh-shiesty-announces-all-eyes-on-shiest-album-drops-new-song-last-man-breathin/ |access-date=2026-08-05 |website=XXL Mag |language=en}}</ref> While incarcerated, his debut studio album, ''[[All Eyes on Shiest]]'' (2026), peaked at number seven on the ''Billboard'' 200.
